ultimately fund only a few ventures, the founders of a new firm should make as
positive an impression on the investor as possible.

The first meeting with an investor is generally very short, about one hour.?°
The investor will typically ask the firm to make a 20- to 30-minute presentation
using PowerPoint slides and use the rest of the time to ask questions. If the
investor is impressed and wants to learn more about the venture, the presen-
